WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Citi Bike Rebalancing Explorer
An independent planning map of where bike-share stations run empty or full.

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:12.500
Imbalance is hard to see, and harder to plan for.

3
00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:18.500
Watch the morning unfold, hour by hour.
Red drains, blue fills · 2,485 stations, Sep 2025 – Aug 2026

4
00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:22.500
By 5 PM, the pattern flips.
The core that filled in the morning now drains

5
00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:27.500
5,849 bikes out of place at 8 AM.
3,154 of them need a truck to deliver: 54% of the imbalance

6
00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:31.100
One switch to Live Docks.
The public live feed, read straight in the browser

7
00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.000
Right now, not an average.
Empty, full and double-outage stations at this moment

8
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:38.600
If it rains: 5,849 → 3,599 bikes out of place.
Less riding, less imbalance. Projected from past weather, and labeled so

9
00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:42.500
Every scenario sits next to the baseline.
Change one input and see what moves

10
00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:46.300
Equity distances you can move.
Defaults: 300 m to NYCHA or a school, more than 800 m to a subway

11
00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:50.000
1,566 of 2,485 stations near NYCHA or a school.
That is 63%, a wide net: tighten it and every count updates

12
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:53.800
Five trucks reach 76 of 1,039 stations short of bikes.
One morning shift each: 20 bikes, at most 45 stops

13
00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:57.500
The stop limit binds, not demand.
Each added truck helps about as much as the first

14
00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:02.500
Ask about any station.
Type a name, or click it on the map

15
00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:07.500
A plain-English briefing, written by AI.
From that station’s own data, for 2,392 stations

16
00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:12.500
One click: the worst stations near NYCHA.
Most often unusable within 300 m of NYCHA housing

17
00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:20.000
Public data, plain methods.

18
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:25.000
Read it as evidence, not a verdict.

19
00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:30.000
See where it hurts and who it hits.
